ng" style=3D"width: 65px; border-radius: 4px;" /> Chris=E2=80=99 Corner=0D=
=0A                            </h2>=0D=0A                            <p cl=
ass=3D"corner-intro">A collection of web design and development news and th=
oughts from CodePen's own Chris Coyier.</p>=0D=0A                          =
</mj-raw>=0D=0A                          <p>Individual fresh CSS features c=
an be amazing, but I always say it=E2=80=99s the most impressive when they =
go <em>together</em>. Adam Argyle knocked one out of the park with his mode=
stly named <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/Lrt6CjYRHt1bjnb4I5n=
xFQ~~/AABEfhA~/lB3gNp8GwKPRbjjS1r2XXOCTP1z6MvbactNtB-wGJkh7zC9Fc-c7waGV0817=
CoJvaJEtMaLeJS61hKf-gssmQf2nNtm3us_Zx8zMJMXp9LPoGPizkPJ5mJow1kVQm7jY">Nice =
Select</a> post &amp; <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/Lrt6CjYR=
Ht1bjnb4I5nxFQ~~/AABEfhA~/lB3gNp8GwKPRbjjS1r2XXOCTP1z6MvbactNtB-wGJkh7zC9Fc=
-c7waGV0817CoJvaJEtMaLeJS61hKf-gssmQf2nNtm3us_Zx8zMJMXp9LPoGPizkPJ5mJow1kVQ=
m7jY">demo</a>. His own post lists all the CSS features that went into it, =
but I=E2=80=99ll do a quick overview.</p>=0D=0A<img src=3D"https://producti=
on-codepen-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=
=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/nice_selects_demo.jpeg" alt=3D"" width=3D=
"400"/>=0D=0A<ul>=0D=0A<li>The core of it is these are =E2=80=9CCustom Sele=
cts=E2=80=9D meaning a native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> element with <cod=
e>appearance: base-select</code> applied. That unlocks the ability to essen=
tially style any part of it any way you want. (By the way, <a href=3D"https=
://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/6LNeX52scbZAEX_jr6Yatg~~/AABEfhA~/MStHzYpu25ln=
_7s3RFKJ-LKCXG7tHICkHJ-jcuMhVgf3qjqLNmWyx6LgQc5fWPD0JpHzIzSbfMCW4ktWuFC3R5r=
oKuPWUMhWfOjfEgwmM0UILWD3CxYLiQprkHrl2L7SChjB7VrfbWnYwOd-jXg27TTnxb5XMqFRDk=
b_YxB47P2OgkMFB_PQxgHfsJOrTLhzAYo1M9BzbV0TwSl25Y4Prw~~">multi-selects are v=
ery close now too</a>.)</li>=0D=0A<li>The opened menu is positioned with an=
chor positioning and have great edge-detection fallbacks.</li>=0D=0A<li>The=
 menus animate both opening and closing thanks to <code>@starting-style</co=
de> and <code>allow-discrete</code> transitions.</li>=0D=0A<li>The scrollin=
g menus have slightly customized scrollbar styles and a subtle animation wh=
ere the fade in from the edges via a <code>view()</code> style scroll-drive=
n animation.</li>=0D=0A<li>Logical properties, color schemes, and user pref=
erences are used so users needs are taken into account.</li>=0D=0A<li>The h=
eaders within the menus are sticky with custom styling when stuck.</li>=0D=
=0A</ul>=0D=0A<p>And honestly, a whole bunch more. Perhaps on their own, ea=
ch of these features is like <em>hey, that=E2=80=99s kinda neat</em>, but w=
hen you start looking at all these CSS improvements combined, you can see h=
ow wildly powerful CSS has become. You might say CSS has become a <a href=
=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/icH5tKmHkrTcQvvM9KPuPA~~/AABEfhA~/cUp=
_i479SIS7Wrmvtzn3vtwqEOOfCQGZre0ITVExI-Ch9q_I1JOuKx7HOqGEg-4Xdik7a84n_YEqC1=
2a0O3Er8tcf6Oij12P08PB6iUBEotsmg4ExZlNAEUQ8HXzNp6rxw8j-XkzZuFKH67r38C_ECAO2=
ZvXq9gKIYmbD4uCONY2vmUBYhTRp25kygA3PyZqUmMWFbiqzAskBs6i1-Cz0g~~">much more =
intelligent language</a>.</p>=0D=0A<p>What do we still want from CSS=3F It=
=E2=80=99s getting harder to think of entirely fresh features that don=E2=
=80=99t have any thought put into them at all yet. For instance, Nathan Kno=
wler=E2=80=99s <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/bGrtooIjZdpDrVQ=
cpne74Q~~/AABEfhA~/JvkpDnMtm10-pZ9PB0tU8xrrEFvJOi7_kRc1_o6ynA6XDuo6wn7sY9d2=
vIu8nLMiwNz_Cx7my-saVzflI9erT_IsUjniXvUL6y79Z_WxaJAwtipSsqmF13Cmeazi2P-zvaN=
RFnVLjbfhtN7a-1j9Xg~~">2026 CSS Wishlist</a> is all stuff that is either he=
re or coming already, and the wish is how they turn CSS into a more cohesiv=
e system. Me, I still really want <code>margin-trim</code> supported everyw=
here, and <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/2rAHFUDkQW9aXGWP8GoY=
PA~~/AABEfhA~/Mck5u9jYbqV9il0LkbMyqjppHUZFQWI__G2O3cb2yIlUUE5K-Re-cxzXtD23Z=
aVsAvgMzEfqEfQ4ZOb6Is1k5fiS3GQbcbvPg74_WOOnW16_GLNGpHMbwgG2skCbWG76a5SQYKDC=
NL8LuqKiDvA52dGAmEDUJsYp-rzfq5ZeuShRUFpA9b5SDKePulFOAwA-lVUBiSZDATn593AKt63=
0kA~~">my 2023 list</a> still had some stuff I=E2=80=99d take. Oh, and I=E2=
=80=99d take like <code>::before-end</code> / <code>::before-begin</code> /=
 <code>::after-end</code> / <code>::after-begin</code> so we=E2=80=99d have=
 both more and more-placeable pseudo elements that mimics <a href=3D"https:=
//go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/64GxCrg5BjhSmWReXz-g5w~~/AABEfhA~/AA_ZfXkBnBu9A=
Z51SZlKSzLrY4a19MttfFfTGfawJJbT90acLWV7OUq2qKyJY7jZYE7yLTDyciTzOSnkoNJWMmLr=
oI7Z92Wbfx6we6jxYayRkMZW5A5YRi1IL-YmvNh01hdbZ80d6eq3xjXDBd7w8dtM8t8jBXXf75S=
GuxyuRtQ8BkVJc85R89Jn4d9Wduw7"><code>insertAdjacentHTML</code></a>. Or <a h=
ref=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/5AkmR7V1Ydb-1mldeREd1Q~~/AABEfhA~/=
LDdejgn5aUpsz3JeawIaMag6-tDN51UJ_0jJooJmwd28D47GrCVLXY9DwWvPMdX31NZfXqI3Gxb=
Zd4CAqDv05-JZdFSVymhDdmiBC-jY8dnDlQT_XodFv2PyyAyPqeGBMsvIVZAbxJ5ohO0njZXfaR=
8_-TOLxCDN2ZOkLWXJBZg~">infinite</a>.</p>=0D=0A<p>Ya know how there used to=
 be lists and roundups and stuff that were like <strong>=E2=80=9CStuff you =
don=E2=80=99t need JavaScript for anymore!!!!!=E2=80=9D</strong>=3F I love =
those, obviously, but I feel like we don=E2=80=99t see them quite as much a=
nymore because HTML and CSS have darn near got it covered now. Like if you =
